D. DO THE SATELLITES RUN LATE? The gauge put through the satellites' own rule (daily anomaly, 15-day running mean,
   the day it passes halfway between its July mean and its mean of 1-22 November and stays above for ten days)
   San Diego: gauge passes halfway on 2026-09-27 (July 6.0, November 33.3 cm); the satellite point at 6800 km on 2026-10-14 (July 4.8, November 29.2); the satellite is 17 days later
   San Francisco: gauge passes halfway on 2026-10-02 (July 4.4, November 31.4 cm); the satellite point at 7600 km on 2026-10-19 (July 5.6, November 26.8); the satellite is 17 days later
   La Libertad (gauge ends 30 September, so no halfway day): the satellite curve best matches the gauge's when slid 9 days later (correlation 0.96)

